'''Hernandez Lee''' (12 April 1997 – 8 March 2021) was a Balboan activist and member of the [[Moviment del poble Birú]] (MPB) who was kidnapped and killed during the [[2021 Carretera Gran Presa del Nord protest]] in [[Tramuntana Province]], [[Balboa]]. Lee's death — he was last seen in the custody of [[Nivell de Seguretat]] security guard [[Jonaes Mendosas i Vidal]] following a confrontation at the protest — became a national controversy and led to the suspension of the road project that the protest had targeted.

== Early life and education ==

Hernandez Lee was born on 12 April 1997 in [[Sant Bart]], [[Jala Province]], to a [[Fosian Balboan people|Zong-Balboan]] family. His father, Tân Siong-lee, was a second-generation Zong-Balboan whose family had emigrated from Sinchew during the Zong Balboa period and had settled in the Sant Bart commercial district. His mother, Lîm Hui-cheng, was a Zong-Balboan from Portnou. Lee grew up in the working-class southwestern districts of Sant Bart, in a neighbourhood with a mixed Zong-Balboan and Black Balboan population.

Lee attended state schools in Sant Bart and enrolled at the [[Universitat de Sant Bart]] in 2016, where he studied environmental science. He became involved in student activism during his university years, participating in campus environmental groups and solidarity campaigns with [[Birú people|Birú]] communities in the Tramuntana highlands. He was described by friends and professors as a quiet, committed student with a particular interest in highland ecology and indigenous land rights.

== Activism ==

Lee joined the [[Moviment del poble Birú]] (MPB) in early 2021, shortly after the announcement of the Nou Gran Presa Carretera project — a proposed road connecting the [[E8 expressway (Balboa)|E8 expressway]] to the [[Gran Presa del Nord]] that would require a tunnel through limestone caves sacred to the Birú people. Lee was drawn to the MPB's decentralised structure and its combination of indigenous rights advocacy and environmental protection, and he began attending MPB assemblies in Sant Bart and travelling to Birú communities in the Tramuntana highlands.

Lee was not himself a member of the Birú community, but his environmental science background and his commitment to indigenous land rights made him an active participant in the movement. He helped organise information campaigns at the Universitat de Sant Bart and participated in planning sessions for the protest at the construction site.

== Death ==

{{main|2021 Carretera Gran Presa del Nord protest}}

On 8 March 2021, Lee travelled to the construction site of the Nou Gran Presa Carretera in the [[La Serra de Llevant]] comarca to participate in the sit-in protest organised by the MPB. During the protest, Lee was involved in a physical altercation with [[Jonaes Mendosas i Vidal]], a security guard employed by [[Nivell de Seguretat]], who had been deployed to the construction site to provide security.

After the protest concluded in the late afternoon, Lee departed the site on foot, intending to walk to [[Sant Jorge, Tramuntana|Sant Jorge]], where he was staying with friends. He was last seen by fellow protesters at approximately 17:30, walking alone along the E8 expressway. According to the subsequent police investigation, Mendosas followed Lee in a NdS vehicle, intercepted him on a remote stretch of the expressway, and forced him into the vehicle.

Lee was reported missing on the morning of 9 March. Mendosas was arrested on 10 March. Lee's body was discovered on 24 March 2021 in a wooded area approximately 8 kilometres east of the construction site. The autopsy determined that the cause of death was blunt force trauma.

== Legacy ==

Lee's death became a rallying point for the [[Moviment del poble Birú]] and the broader indigenous rights and environmental movements in Balboa. His name was invoked during the [[2026 Balboa data center protests]], where MPB activists cited his death as an example of the dangers faced by indigenous rights activists and the consequences of private security deployments at protest sites.

The Hernandez Lee Foundation, established by his family in 2022, provides scholarships for Birú students at the Universitat de Sant Bart and supports indigenous land rights advocacy in the Tramuntana highlands.

